==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|bitterli}}, {{m|enm|biterli}}, {{m|enm|biterliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|biterlīċe}}, {{m|ang|bitterlīċe|t=bitterly}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|bitter|ly}}. Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|bitterlik|t=bitterly}}, {{cog|de|bitterlich|t=bitterly}}, {{cog|sv|bitterligen|t=bitterly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪtəɹli/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪtəli/}}
* {{hyph|en|bit|ter|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bitterly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[bitter]] manner.
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=4|passage=Judge Short had gone to town, and Farrar was off for a three days' cruise up the lake. I was '''bitterly''' regretting I had not gone with him when the distant notes of a coach horn reached my ear, and I descried a four-in-hand winding its way up the inn road from the direction of Mohair.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Johanna Spyri
|by=Eileen Hall
|title=Heidi
|year=1956
|origyear=1880
|page=91
|passage=Heidi threw herself down beside Clara's chair and began to cry '''bitterly'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 1, 2011|author=Phil McNulty|work=BBC Sport
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/15045708.stm Everton 0-2 Liverpool]
|passage=Liverpool's £58m strikeforce of {{w|Andy Carroll}} and {{w|Luis Suarez}} scored the goals that settled the {{w|Merseyside derby}} at {{w|Goodison Park}} - but {{w|Everton F.C.|Everton}} were left complaining '''bitterly''' about {{w|Jack Rodwell}}'s controversial early red card.}}
# {{cap|extremely}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=December 1 2023|author=Emma Sanders|title=England 3-2 Netherlands|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67577192|passage=On a '''bitterly''' cold evening at Wembley, the Lionesses knew only victory would be enough to keep alive Team GB's hopes of competing in Paris.}}

